{"id": "holcim-2026-10-23-018", "date": "2026-10-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["holcim"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings", "guidance"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Holcim updates earnings guidance for 2026 following sales growth in first nine months", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/news/Holcim_2021_Logo_Wall_1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>Switzerland:</strong> Holcim’s net sale rose by 5.7% year-on-year to €13.7bn in the first nine months of 2026, from €12.9bn in the same period in 2025. Recurring earnings before interest and taxation (EBIT) grew by 6.1% to €2.62bn from €2.47bn. Sales from the building materials product line increased by 1.4% to €9.66bn, but those from the building materials solution line increased by 14.1% to €", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/21407-holcim-updates-earnings-guidance-for-2026-following-sales-growth-in-first-nine-months", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "ultratech-2026-10-23-019", "date": "2026-10-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["ultratech"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["raw_material_energy_cost", "capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["涉及產能"]}, "title": "UltraTech Cement commissions 3.3Mt/yr Petnikota cement plant", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/UltraTech-Cement-Baga-cement-plant-1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>India:</strong> UltraTech Cement has commissioned its new US$279m, 3.3Mt/yr Petnikota cement plant in Andhra Pradesh's Nandyal district. The plant will produce composite cements using ground granulated blast furnace slag (GGBFS) and fly ash. The Press Trust of India has reported that the plant has an additional 0.3Mt/yr of cement grinding capacity and is designed to be able to use 100% ", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/21406-ultratech-cement-commissions-3-3mt-yr-petnikota-cement-plant", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-23-020", "date": "2026-10-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["涉及產能"]}, "title": "Conch Investment Holding and Hope Global Investment break ground on 1Mt/yr Malibé cement plant", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/conch-cement-electric-vehicles-1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>Gabon:</strong> China-based Conch Investment Holding and Hope Global Investment have commenced construction of their upcoming US$195m, 1Mt/yr Malibé cement plant in Estuaire. The La Tribune newspaper has reported that the companies will jointly build, finance and operate the plant. It will serve Gabon’s domestic market when operational.</p>", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/21403-conch-investment-holding-and-hope-global-investment-break-ground-on-1mt-yr-malibe-cement-plant", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-23-021", "date": "2026-10-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["record", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Afrimat publishes six-month 2027 financial year results", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/South-Africa-Table-Mountian-1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>South Africa:</strong> Afrimat recorded sales of US$309m in the six months up to the end of August 2026, the first half of its 2027 financial year (FY 2027). This corresponds to a year-on-year decline of 4%. Alliance News has reported that the producer attributed the decline to the performance of its cement business, alongside other units. Afrimat's pretax profit fell by 48%, to US$8.36m.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/21402-afrimat-publishes-six-month-2027-financial-year-results", "type": "rss"}]}
